# Large vendored binaries under prebuilt/ are committed as REGULAR git blobs
# (NO Git LFS): GitHub forbids LFS object uploads to public forks, and this
# repo's remote is a public fork. To stay under GitHub's 100MB/file hard limit,
# the two big archives are stored as <=90MB split parts:
#   prebuilt/gradle/gradle-8.14.5-bin.zip.part00/.part01   (was 132MB)
#   prebuilt/gradle-cache/modules-2.tar.gz.part00/.part01  (was 158MB)
# The build scripts (bootstrap-gradle.sh / restore-cache.sh) reassemble them
# with `cat ...part*`. The *.so files are each <25MB and go in as-is.
#
# Mark all binary types -text so git never applies CRLF conversion (the working
# copy sits on a Samba mount reached from Windows).

prebuilt/**/*.so     -text
prebuilt/**/*.aar    -text
prebuilt/**/*.jar    -text
prebuilt/**/*.zip    -text
prebuilt/**/*.tar.gz -text
prebuilt/**/*.part*  -text

# Ensure shell scripts keep Unix line endings (the repo is built on Linux;
# the Windows working copy is on a Samba mount and must not introduce CRLF).
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.kts  text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
